<mei xmlns="http://www.music-encoding.org/ns/mei" meiversion="5.0"><meiHead xml:lang="en"><fileDesc><titleStmt><title>Rhe 2-132v-a-38</title></titleStmt><pubStmt><identifier>https://corpus-monodicum.de/d/2903a397-1751-48ab-aac5-c51cb18a7473</identifier><respStmt><corpName role="publisher">Corpus Monodicum</corpName></respStmt><address><addrLine>Domerschulstraße 13</addrLine><addrLine>97070 Würzburg</addrLine></address><availability><useRestrict auth.uri="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/">CC BY-NC 4.0</useRestrict></availability><date isodate="2026-11-04"/></pubStmt><seriesStmt><title>Corpus Monodicum</title><respStmt><resp>Edition (Spiele)</resp><persName>Elaine Stratton Hild</persName></respStmt><funder>Akademie der Wissenschaften und der Literatur Mainz</funder></seriesStmt><notesStmt><annot type="global-comment"><table><tr><td><rend>The Exhortatio virtutum and the Ordo virtutum include personages and themes that occur earlier in Scivias.

For example,
Scivias Book 2, Vision 7 describes the devil bound. 
In the Exhortatio virtutum, virtues bind the devil in the chants Ligate ergo, O regina nostra, and Gaudete o socii. 
In the Ordo virtutum, the chants O victoria que, O fortissimi, O dulcissima bellatrix, Ligate ergo, O regina nostra, and Gaudete o socii describe the same actions.

Scivias Book 1, Vision 4 presents a lament of a pilgrim soul struggling to resist the devil (Querela anime de via erroris)—the same drama that forms the primary subject of the Exhortatio virtutum and the Ordo virtutum. Both the EV and the OV include a lament of pilgrim souls, Querela animarum in carne positarum. 

Personified virtues (the primary personages in the Exhortatio virtutum and the Ordo virtutum) appear earlier in Scivias in:
Book 1, Vision 2, Section 33
Book 3, Vision 3
Book 3, Vision 4, Section 15
Book 3, Vision 6
Book 3, Vision 8 (with the first seven virtues corresponding to the order they appear in the Ordo virtutum)
Book 3, Vision 9
Book 3, Vision 10
Among these personified virtues, Humility takes a prominent role, as in the Exhortatio virtutum and the Ordo virtutum.</rend></td></tr></table></annot></notesStmt><sourceDesc><source xml:id="wit-rhe-2"><bibl><identifier type="siglum">Rhe 2</identifier></bibl></source></sourceDesc></fileDesc><encodingDesc><appInfo><application version="0.9.1"><name>Monodi-Zero</name></application></appInfo></encodingDesc><workList><work><identifier>Rhe 2-132v-a-38</identifier><title>O splendidissima gemma</title><incip><incipText><p>O splendidissima gemma</p></incipText></incip><contents><contentItem><locus from="132v-a">f. 132v-a, l. 38</locus></contentItem></contents><classification><termList><term type="genre">Spiele-Passus</term><term type="Editor">Elaine Stratton Hild</term><term type="Endseite">132v-b</term><term type="Referenz_auf_Spiel">Rhe 2-132v-a-38S</term><term type="Endzeile">9</term><term type="Zusatz_zu_Textinitium">Ohne Notation</term><term type="SpielName">Exhortatio virtutum, Scivias Book III Vision 13</term><term type="Band_Genre">Spiele</term></termList></classification></work></workList><manifestationList><manifestation><identifier type="siglum">Rhe 2</identifier><titleStmt><title>Rhe 2</title></titleStmt><creation><geogName role="origin-region">Quellen deutscher Herkunft</geogName><corpName role="origin-institution">Monastery - Rupertsberg</corpName></creation><langUsage><language xml:lang="la"/></langUsage><classification><termList><term type="ordenstradition">Benedictine</term></termList></classification><itemList><item><identifier type="shelfmark">Hs. 2, Riesencodex</identifier><physLoc><repository><geogName role="settlement">Wiesbaden</geogName><corpName>Hochschul- und Landesbibliothek RheinMain</corpName></repository></physLoc></item></itemList></manifestation></manifestationList><revisionDesc><change isodate="2026-11-04"><changeDesc><p>Exported with Monodi-Zero 0.9.1.</p></changeDesc></change></revisionDesc></meiHead><music><body><mdiv type="main"><score><scoreDef><staffGrp><staffDef n="1" notationtype="neume" lines="5" clef.shape="G" clef.line="2"/></staffGrp></scoreDef><section xml:id="m-0979f1db-9053-4715-a4e6-7f098bc312d8"><section xml:id="m-87d033b0-fcd7-4fac-bb1a-6d56f5a3595f"/><section xml:id="m-1a418e17-b141-456c-b174-db450673ab3d"/><section xml:id="m-230a56d4-1123-44ee-8891-44cfee8ef3d1"><section xml:id="m-cc42a638-d70f-46b1-9239-54558fbd36fc"><section xml:id="m-40c5c2d4-4de1-412c-8832-684810a6f676"/></section></section><section xml:id="m-f43d5aab-a5c7-4ae7-81ea-d6c86c34d7c4"><section xml:id="m-61a1ecde-54a7-44a8-ba3d-aff53a395b46"><section xml:id="m-cf25a35a-c8f3-4730-9ab4-097cb73b8abe"><sb xml:id="m-ab4a6568-9b53-430f-8d60-f13bfdbe3ad6"/><staff n="1"><layer n="1"><annot xml:id="m-d68b1806-5e77-4dfc-9597-8eeef235f3fb" type="paratext" label="Formteil">TERCIA DECIMA UISIO TERCIĘ PARTIS (f. 132v-a)</annot><annot xml:id="m-7a20d4f5-f0e6-47d7-bce8-2a703cd70e75" type="paratext" label="Formteil">DEINDE UIDI LUCIDISSIMUM AEREM
IN QUO AUDIUI IN OMNIBUS PREDICTIS SIGNIFICATIONIBUS MIRABILI MODO DIUERSUM GENUS MUSICORUM IN LAUDIBUS CIUIUM SUPERNORUM GAUDIORUM IN UIA UERITATIS FORTITER PERSEUERANTIUM
AC IN QUERELIS REUOCATORUM AD LAUDES EORUNDEM GAUDIORUM
ET IN EXHORTATIONE UIRTUTUM SE EXHORTANTIUM AD SALUTEM POPULORUM
QUIBUS DIABOLICĘ INSIDIĘ REPUGNANT
SED IPSE UIRTUTES EAS OPPRIMUNT
ITA TAMEN QUOD SIC FIDELES HOMINES TANDEM A PECCATIS AD SUPERNA PER PENITENTIAM TRANSEUNT
</annot><annot xml:id="m-06c4aa13-e864-4eff-9837-dfb493af6081" type="paratext" label="Aufführung">ET SONUS ILLE UT UOX MULTITUDINIS 
IN LAUDIBUS DE SUPERNIS GRADIBUS IN ARMONIA SIMPHONIZANS 
